<html>
	<head>
		<script>
			sessionStorage.redirect = location.href;
		  </script>
		  <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0;URL='/'">
	</head>
	<body>
		<!-- This is empty, but the code in the <head> section will redirect as 301 to the root URL.  Then there's some code in index.html which will reconstruct the full path.  This came from https://www.smashingmagazine.com/2016/08/sghpa-single-page-app-hack-github-pages/, which also says how this page must be >=512 bytes, which it is...now! -->
	</body>
</html>